---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Uses"
  description="Hardware, software, and editor setup that earns its place."
  lede="Tools that earn their place. Anything not on this list got tried and dropped."
  nav="home"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Hardware</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>MacBook Pro M-series, 32 GB.</li>
      <li>Stream Deck XL — wired to <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/govee-light-management">my Govee plugin</a> for room lights + meeting modes.</li>
      <li>External 4K monitor, mechanical keyboard, ergonomic mouse.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Editor + terminal</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Claude Code</strong> with the caveman skill for output compression and the roady MCP server for plan-of-record.</li>
      <li><strong>Zed</strong> for quick edits; <strong>Neovim</strong> for everything serious.</li>
      <li><strong>Ghostty</strong> terminal, <strong>zsh</strong> with my own dotfiles.</li>
      <li><strong>Homebrew</strong> for everything else.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Engineering stack</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Go</strong> for services and CLIs (<a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/roady">roady</a>, <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/tokenops">tokenops</a>, <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/mnemos">mnemos</a>).</li>
      <li><strong>Astro</strong> for static sites (this one).</li>
      <li><strong>SQLite</strong> first; PostgreSQL only when SQLite stops scaling.</li>
      <li><strong>MCP</strong> as the integration substrate for AI tooling.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Productivity</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Roady</strong> — every project I touch has a plan-of-record. Survives context resets.</li>
      <li><strong>Mnemos</strong> — long-term memory the assistant can read back across sessions.</li>
      <li><strong>iA Writer</strong> for drafting prose.</li>
      <li><strong>Cal.com</strong> for booking; <strong>Fastmail</strong> for email.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="muted">
      <em>Format inspired by <a href="https://uses.tech">uses.tech</a>.</em>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
